{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0121Xyw2SqinmQzGg5G71YDD","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D17 post-run, 2026-10-18)\n2:\n3:Scope: what a D18+ `evidence.zip` group (or backfilled old-group id) could be, how we would recognise it, which standard tool answers it, and how ready we\n4:are. Grounded in `reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` (lane log D1-D17), `challenges/day17/binary-decoder-ring/solver/`,\n5:`lib/binary.py` (`hcfg_scan`/`hcfg_find`, `packer_info`, `unpack_upx`, `go_buildinfo`, `go_pclntab_funcs`, `rustfilt`, `macho_facts`,\n6:`recover_return_constants`, `ghidra_decompile`, `jar_app_classes`, `wasm_layout`) and `tests/data/binary_fixtures/TARGETS.json` (all 9 targets have fixtures).\n7:\n8:Progression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\n9:language); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix from the file-name tag (C ELF\n10:`stripped`/`symbolized`; WebAssembly `compact`/`direct`, labels `wasm`/`wasm32`); D17 \"Decoder Ring\" = back to ONE new language\n11:(Ada/GNAT ELF, HCFG RAW in `.rodata`, nothing new to decode) + BACKFILL #2 (160 -> 204 ids, 11 per old group) that re-asked\n12:EARLIER DAYS' single-solve facts (d01 marker/recover_code, d02 mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol, d04 has_go_runtime, d05\n13:has_rust_mangled_symbol, d06 methods/access_flags, d07 method_count/has_coroutine_runtime) and a NEW label field `hcfg_storage`\n14:(an ENUM after the organizers' mid-day contract revision: base64 / raw_hcfg_section / raw_const_array / wasm_data_segment / raw,\n15:picked by an ordered rule list in the question text; before the revision ~10.9k free-text probes failed). TT/Mastery: d01 re-rolled\n16:STRIPPED -> `recover_code` `none`. Lessons for D18+: (a) the next backfill will most likely\n17:reach D8-D17's own day facts (Swift/Nim/Zig/D/FPC/Crystal/ObjC/pair/wasm/Ada identity booleans, symbol names, class/selector\n18:lists, wasm imports/exports) -- the \"theme\" of a day is answerable LATER on its old group; (b) the new-day member keeps being a\n19:plain ELF whose ids the carried-over solver already answers (D17 group banked at T+18 s); (c) label fields with no derivable\n20:spelling (`hcfg_storage` raw, D3 `pe_cli`) are the real time sink -- and the organizers fix them by REVISING THE CONTRACT\n21:(enum + rule text), so re-pull it instead of guessing; (d) location/storage-classification fields (`hcfg_offset`,\n22:`hcfg_storage`) need offset -> section/segment mapping on every container. Asked field names: config_*, format, machine, architecture,\n23:elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols, section_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*,\n24:has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags,\n25:method_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset, hcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods.\n26:Remaining risks: (1) more per-language fact backfills, (2) a twist that hides the HCFG from a byte scan (the D17 \"decoder\" theme\n27:did not materialise but stays plausible: packing, real crypto, stack-built, per-string encryption, API hashing), (3) a new\n28:container/arch label (Mach-O, eBPF, AArch64...), (4) more pair days with `_`-containing tags.\n29:\n30:Tool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\n31:Installed: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\n32:llvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\n33:rizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\n34:AARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\n35:jadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara, wabt (wasm-objdump/wasm2wat/wat2wasm/wasm-decompile), floss (.venv), luac,\n36:7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\n37:lz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only).\n38:Missing: qemu-user(-static), wasm-ld/lld, wasmtime, capa, Detect-It-Easy (diec), de4dot, monodis, erlang (beam_disasm),\n39:unluac/luajit-decompiler (luac present), blutter, srecord (srec_cat), binutils-multiarch, checksec, python zstandard/brotli, rzpipe/r2pipe.\n40:\n41:## Concept table\n42:\n43:| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D18+ likelihood |\n44:|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n45:| 1 | C ELF (gcc, glibc) | seen D1, D15 (+ every day's d01; D17 re-asked marker/recover_code) | `GCC: (...)` in `.comment`, `.interp` ld-linux, `__libc_start_main` | [I] `readelf -hSW f; readelf -sW f; objdump -d -M intel f` | high (carry-over every day; ma\n46:| 2 | C++ Itanium ELF / MinGW PE32+ | seen D2 | `_Z` symbols, `_ZTV`/`_ZTI`/`_ZTS`, `libstdc++`; PE `.text$_Z...` COMDAT, `.CRT`, `.tls` | [I] `nm -C f`; `objdump -t f.exe`; `c++filt` | high (carry-over; ELF/PE re-rolls per member) |\n47:| 3 | .NET C# PE (pe_cli) | seen D3 | `BSJB` metadata root `v4.0.30319`, `mscoree.dll`/`_CorExeMain`, `.runtimeconfig.json` | [I] `ilspycmd f.dll`; python `dnfile` | high (carry-over) |\n48:| 4 | Go (static, stripped; PE in Mastery) | seen D4 | `\\xff Go buildinf:`, `.gopclntab`, `runtime.`, `go1.NN` | [I] `GoReSym -t -d -p f`; `go version -m f`; `lib.binary.go_buildinfo` | high (carry-over) |\n49:| 5 | Rust ELF (debug_info) | seen D5 | `_ZN...17h<16hex>E` / `_