{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MfxnoqDSeFqK26ub21gzaL","type":"tool_result","content":"    data_segments (file_offset + mem_offset); wasm-objdump -x F ; HCFG RAW in data seg 0 -> raw scan finds it (crc-gate)\n  ':10' text lines => Intel HEX ; 'S0'/'S1' => S-record ; no magic + ARM vector table => raw firmware (rizin -m base)\nSTEP 2  rz-bin -I F   (or readelf -hlSW F)  -> lang, machine, bits, endian, static, stripped, pic, relro, nx, canary\n  e_machine: 3 x86 | 62 x86-64 | 40 ARM | 183 AArch64 | 8 MIPS | 20 PPC | 21 PPC64 | 243 RISC-V | 2/43 SPARC\n  labels: GM-confirmed x86-64/x86/AArch64/ARM (ELF), i386/x86-64 (PE); others = readelf spelling first, then EM_ name minus\n  prefix; kind:integer => decimal e_machine. Dispatch on answer_format.kind, never on field name.\n  no .symtab => stripped (answer [] / none / false); no INTERP => static; ET_DYN+INTERP => PIE; ET_REL => object file\n  UPX0/UPX1 sections or \"UPX!\" or entropy>7.2 => PACKED: upx -t F; cp F /tmp/x; upx -d /tmp/x (fix zeroed UPX! first)\nSTEP 3  strings -a -n6 F | grep -m8 -E 'GCC:|clang|rustc|go1\\.|GHC |OCaml|caml_|FPC |Crystal|zig|GNAT Version|gfortran|DMD|Nim|\n        swift|_kDart|kfun:|__svm|MEI|nuitka|AU3!|Borland|MSVBVM|libcob|UPX|HCFG|SENGR'   -> toolchain + blob form\n  toolchain -> tool: Go GoReSym -t -d -p | Rust rustfilt | .NET ilspycmd | jar javap -v -p / jadx | Swift swift-demangle\n  Nim nim-demangle | PyInstaller pyinstxtractor+pycdc | AutoIt autoit-ripper | anything else: rizin -q -c 'aaa;afl' /\n  analyzeHeadless (lib.binary.ghidra_decompile) | foreign arch: rizin -a <arch> / llvm-objdump-18 / Ghidra (no exec, qemu absent)\nHCFG (every new member since D2)\n  python: from lib.binary import hcfg_find, hcfg_scan; hcfg_find(open(F,'rb').read())  -> config, offset, encoding, key, crc_ok\n  raw magic 'HCFG' | b64 'SENGR' | hex '48434647' | rot13 'FRATE' | b64-zlib 'eJ' | b64-gzip 'H4sI' -> covered by hcfg_scan\n  accept only crc32(plain)==header crc AND JSON parses; keep scanning past decoys (D9 had two raw-magic decoys)\n  NOT FOUND => blob is hidden: (1) packed? unpack; (2) AES S-box 637c777b / TEA 9e3779b9 / 'expand 32-byte k' => find key+IV\n  near the call, decrypt with pycryptodome; (3) runs of mov [rbp-x], imm => stack-built: collect imms with capstone or\n  emulate the builder with unicorn; (4) PE .rsrc / .NET resource / jar non-class entry / overlay past last section;\n  (5) .init_array / TLS callback decoder => emulate it. Offsets: raw=the H, base64=the S (GM-confirmed); else first stored byte.\nFIELDS: format = container only (elf/pe/macho?/jar; .NET pe_cli) | machine/architecture = container machine word |\n  qualifier ids dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field> -> member whose file name has <tag> (D15 stripped/symbolized, D16 compact/direct;\n  match the LONGEST member-name token, a tag may contain `_`) ; sha256_K = zip archive order | config_* verbatim from HCFG JSON |\n  has_<x>_section = literal section name | hex fields lowercase 0x | never chase the prompt's theme: answer only asked ids.\n  D17 Ada ELF (GNAT 14.2): plain ELF, HCFG RAW in .rodata -> carried-over solver answers it unchanged.\nBACKFILL ids on OLD groups (D8, D17): an unknown field on dNN = that day's own facts. Seen: marker (.huntress string),\n  recover_code (decimal imm), mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol (bare _ZNK.../_ZTI...; PE .text$/.rdata$), has_go_runtime,\n  has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime (enum true/false), methods (Main-Class method_info names incl <init>, JSON),\n  access_flags (decimal, 49), method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>). Derive from bytes, POST all derivable ones together.\nhcfg_storage (enum): base64 carrier -> base64 | literal HCFG in section `.hcfg` -> raw_hcfg_section | in WASM data seg ->\n  wasm_data_segment | in another native data section (.data/.rodata) -> raw_const_array | else raw. Stripped d01 => recover_code none.\nUNGUESSABLE label: ~10 single-id probes max, HELP.md, then re-pull the contract (organizers revise it: enum + rule text).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"hcfg-storage-classifier\", \"concept\": \"Generic `hcfg_storage` token for EVERY group/container per the D17 GM rule list (base64 / raw_hcfg_section / wasm_data_segment / raw_const_array / raw)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 asked it on d08/d09/d11-d14 only; the next backfill likely spreads it (as hcfg_offset spread) to d02 (ELF `.hcfg` or PE `.hcfg` COFF section), d03\n  {\"id\": \"question-rule-extractor\", \"concept\": \"Read the contract's per-id rule text + `accepted_values` and enforce it pre-submit (organizer revisions turn labels into enums)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17: the organizers re-issued the contract mid-day; hcfg_storage became kind enum with accepted_values and 'Apply these mutually exclusive rules in order: <token> when <cond>\n  {\"id\": \"offset-section-mapper\", \"concept\": \"Map a file offset to its container location: ELF section + segment (name, flags, VA), PE section (name, RVA, VA), Mach-O segment,section, WASM data segment index + memory offset\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Underpins hcfg_storage and the likely next location ids (`hcfg_section`, `hcfg_va`/`hcfg_vaddr`, `hcfg_rva`, `hcfg_segment`, `\n  {\"id\": \"elf-header-segment-facts\", \"concept\": \"Remaining ELF header + program-header facts as fields: e_flags, os_abi, abi_version, e_phnum/e_shnum/e_shstrndx, segments list (p_type order), interpreter, GNU_STACK/RELRO/PIE/static booleans\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Backfills so far asked elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, section_names, symbols, has_symtab. Next\n  {\"id\": \"ada-gnat-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"Ada/GNAT facts for the d17 group when its own theme is backfilled: GNAT version, binder/elaboration symbols, Ada subprogram names, decoder function, exception ids\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 prompt ('recover the reversible decoder') was unasked; the D17 backfill pattern means d17 facts get asked within days. From the cached Ada \n  {\"id\": \"fortran-gfortran-member\", \"concept\": \"Fortran (gfortran) ELF as a new-day member: identity cues, facts, HCFG in a COMMON block / module data / DATA statement\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Language order so far skipped Fortran/COBOL/Haskell/OCaml; Fortran is the cheapest for organizers after Ada (gcc front-end, dynamic glibc like D17). Cues: `libgfortran.so.5` NEEDED, \n  {\"id\": \"contract-revision-watch\", \"concept\": \"Organizers revise the live contract mid-day (D17: exact_text -> enum + rule text)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"When an exact_text label resists ~10 probes: write HELP, then re-pull the contract (`hctf status <id>`) every ~20-30 min and diff question text/answer_format per id; D17 the revision converted ~3.5 h and ~10.9k rejected prob\n  {\"id\": \"qemu-user-static\", \"concept\": \"Run/observe foreign-arch ELF decoders (ARM/AArch64/MIPS/PPC/RISC-V)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install qemu-user-static binfmt-support (only qemu-system-* are installed now). Use only inside the bwrap sandbox, never on the host; static analysis remains the default.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"diec\", \"concept\": \"Compiler/packer/language fingerprint for unknown toolchains\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release horsicq/DIE-engine (die_lin64_portable tar) -> `diec -j F`. Complements `rz-bin -I` lang= and the STEP 3 strings regex when a new language lands.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"checksec-fields\", \"concept\": \"PIE/RELRO/NX/canary/static as answer fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"`rz-bin -I` already prints pic/relro/nx/canary/static/stripped. GM spelling unknown: relro full/partial/none, booleans true/false like has_symtab. Add to playbook naming law before first sighting; no checksec install needed.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-language-fingerprints\", \"concept\": \"Haskell, OCaml, Fortran, V, Odin, COBOL, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka (Ada seen D17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Cue strings are in the Recognition cues STEP 3 regex. All still answer format=elf/architecture=x86-64 per the D8-D15 law; risk is only where the HCFG literal lives (compressed Dart snapshot, Nuitka constants blob, GH\n  {\"id\": \"de4dot\", \"concept\": \"ConfuserEx / .NET string encryption\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github de4dot-cex (ViRb3) release; needs apt mono-runtime. `de4dot F -o clean.dll` then ilspycmd.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"erlang-lua-decompilers\", \"concept\": \"BEAM, Lua, LuaJIT bytecode\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"luac (lua5.4) is now installed. Still missing: apt erlang-base (beam_lib/beam_disasm), unluac jar (sourceforge), luajit-decompiler-v2 (github marsinator358) -- only if a bytecode container appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"binutils-multiarch\", \"concept\": \"objdump/readelf for MIPS/PPC/SPARC/RISC-V\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install binutils-multiarch; rizin, llvm-objdump-18 and Ghidra already cover disassembly, so this is a convenience only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ihex-srec-firmware\", \"concept\": \"Intel HEX / S-record / raw firmware members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"objcopy -I ihex|srec -O binary already converts (srecord not needed). For raw blobs: rizin -a arm -b 16 -m <base>; format label unknown (`ihex`/`srec`/`raw`?) -> submit alone.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"haskell-ghc-member\", \"concept\": \"Haskell (GHC) static ELF: z-encoded closures, rts strings, HCFG as a ByteString literal (raw or base64) possibly split across closures\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `hs_main`, `ghczmprim_GHCziTypes_`, `base_GHCziBase_` z-encoding (zi = '.', zm = '-'), `GHC 9.x` rts banner, huge static binary, `.data` closures. Facts: has_ghc_runt\n  {\"id\": \"ocaml-native-member\", \"concept\": \"OCaml native ELF (ocamlopt): caml symbols, string literals with OCaml block headers, HCFG offset convention\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `caml_startup`, `caml_main`, `camlStdlib__`, `camlDune__exe__Main`, `OCAMLRUNPARAM`. OCaml strings are header-prefixed blocks (word header + padded bytes, last byte = pad count) -> HCFG raw st\n  {\"id\": \"kotlin-native-member\", \"concept\": \"Kotlin/Native ELF (konanc): `kfun:` symbols, Konan runtime, HCFG in an object literal\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Kotlin already appeared as a jar (D7); a native build is a plausible 'pair the language with a new container' twist. Cues: `kfun:` / `kclass:` / `ktype:` symbols, `Konan_main`, `Kotlin_` runtime, `kotlin.native.internal\n  {\"id\": \"pe-optional-header-facts\", \"concept\": \"PE/COFF facts for the PE members (d02 MinGW, d03 .NET, d10 Zig PE, d04 Go .exe): subsystem, image_base, timestamp, characteristics, dll_characteristics, section names (NUL-trimmed), entry RVA/VA, imports\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PE members re-roll into Mastery for d02/d04/d10; a backfill on them would ask the ELF-equivalent \n  {\"id\": \"cobol-gnucobol-member\", \"concept\": \"GnuCOBOL ELF (cobc): libcob NEEDED, cob_init, PIC X working-storage holding the HCFG\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `libcob.so.4` NEEDED, `cob_init`/`cob_module_enter`, `GnuCOBOL` strings, program-id symbols upper-case. WORKING-STORAGE `PIC X(n) VALUE` literals sit raw in `.data` (-> raw_const_array) but COBOL source limits lit\n  {\"id\": \"dart-aot-snapshot\", \"concept\": \"Dart AOT executable (`dart compile exe`): snapshot sections, HCFG inside the isolate snapshot (possibly compressed/obfuscated)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `_kDartVmSnapshotData`, `_kDartIsolateSnapshotData/Instructions` symbols, `Dart_` runtime strings, ELF appended to dartaotruntime (or a standalone ELF in recent SDKs). Strings\n  {\"id\": \"backfill-language-identity-facts\", \"concept\": \"Per-language identity + theme facts for the D8-D17 groups (the next backfill): has_<lang>_runtime / has_<lang>_mangled_symbol / class, protocol, selector, proc, template names\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 re-asked D1-D7's single-solve facts on their old groups (marker, recover_code, mangled\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-classfile-facts\", \"concept\": \"Full JVM ClassFile facts for jar groups (d06/d07): versions, constant-pool count, this/super/interfaces, fields, methods+descriptors, attributes, Kotlin metadata\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 asked methods (names, table order, incl <init>), access_flags (decimal 49) and method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-metadata-facts\", \"concept\": \".NET metadata facts for the d03 group: assembly name/version, MVID, TypeDef/MethodDef names, FieldRVA, TargetFramework, entry point token\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). d03 is the only old group whose day-facts were not re-asked on D17 (it got hcfg_version/xor_key_hex only); a later backfill likely asks typ\n  {\"id\": \"decoder-routine-locator\", \"concept\": \"Locate and characterise the config DECODER in the binary: function name, algorithm (xor/add/rol/rc4...), key/immediate, loop length, references to the stored blob\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 prompt: 'Recover the reversible decoder' (unasked, but a later backfill may ask decoder facts on d17 or any \n  {\"id\": \"native-imports-exports-facts\", \"concept\": \"imports / NEEDED / interpreter / exports lists for ELF, PE, Mach-O\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Generic facts: ELF `needed` (DT_NEEDED order), `imports` (UND .dynsym names, table order, version suffix stripped), `interpreter` (.interp without NUL), `exports` (defined dynsyms); PE import dll list + \n  {\"id\": \"provenance-facts-extractor\", \"concept\": \"Build provenance fields: GNU build-id, .comment compiler banner, DWARF producer/language/comp_dir, PE TimeDateStamp/PDB path/Rich, Go/Rust toolchain version\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Implement in the facts dict so a new id answers without code: build_id = lowercase hex of NT_GNU_BUILD_ID desc (no \n  {\"id\": \"language-detector\", \"concept\": \"lib.binary.language_of(data) -> source language/toolchain token with evidence, for all 17 seen languages + next candidates\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). A `language`/`compiler`/`toolchain` id on any group would need consistent tokens: c, cpp, csharp/dotnet, go, rust, java, kotlin, swift, nim, zig, d, pascal/fp\n  {\"id\": \"emulate-return-value\", \"concept\": \"Recover a function's return value by emulation when it is not a `mov eax, imm; ret` leaf (obfuscated/computed/OLLVM recover_code)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). recover_code was re-asked D17; a mutated variant may compute the constant (xor of two imms, lookup table, flattened switch). unicorn x86-64 (install\n  {\"id\": \"api-hashing-resolver\", \"concept\": \"Imports resolved by hash (ROR13, djb2, FNV-1a, CRC32, murmur) -> resolved API list / hash algorithm fields\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Natural 'encoded' sequel to D17 for a decoder-themed day. Precompute hash tables for libc/kernel32/ntdll export names under the common algorithms; scan .rodata/.text immed\n  {\"id\": \"per-string-encryption\", \"concept\": \"Every string (not just HCFG) encrypted individually with a shared decoder (xor/add per string, stack strings) -> decoded string lists as fields\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Escalation of the D17 'encoded configuration' theme: config fields stored as separate xor'd strings instead of one HCFG blob. Use flo\n  {\"id\": \"build-pair-router\", \"concept\": \"Same-source build PAIRS beyond stripped/symbolized and compact/direct (static/dynamic, O0/O2/Os, pie/nopie, debug/release, packed/unpacked, plain/obfuscated)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D15 and D16 were both 'one source, two builds' with `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` ids. Fixtures: gcc -O0 vs -O2, -static vs \n  {\"id\": \"cross-arch-pair\", \"concept\": \"Same source built for x86-64 + AArch64 (+ RISC-V/ARM .o) as a pair, arch-named qualifiers\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15 links, clang-18 --target=riscv64/armv7 -c gives ET_REL. Name tags like `-x86_64.elf`/`-aarch64.elf`/`-arm64` put an UNDERSCORE inside the qualifier (`d17_analysis_x86_6\n  {\"id\": \"wasm-inventory-fields\", \"concept\": \"WASM 'doors' as answer fields: imports, exports, memory min/max/shared/memory64, table + elem (call_indirect targets), start, globals, data segment count/offsets, custom sections\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). The D16 prompt named imports/memory/indirect calls but asked none; carry-over backfill may add the\n  {\"id\": \"ebpf-object\", \"concept\": \"eBPF ELF object (e_machine 247) with HCFG in .rodata / a map section\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). clang-18 -target bpf -O2 -c fixture with SEC(\\\"xdp\\\"), a `license` section, `.maps`, and an HCFG `.hcfg`/`.rodata` blob. Targets: format `elf`, elf_type ET_REL, machine readelf spelling `Linux BPF` (EM_BPF; integer 247\n  {\"id\": \"sstrip-corrupt-headers\", \"concept\": \"ELF without section headers (sstrip, e_shnum=0) or with bogus e_shoff/e_shstrndx/fake section names\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixtures: gcc build then python-zero e_shoff/e_shnum/e_shstrndx; another with garbage e_shstrndx; another with a section renamed to `.hcfg` that does not hold the blob. Targets\n  {\"id\": \"wasm-hcfg-hidden\", \"concept\": \"WASM HCFG not a plain active data segment: custom section `hcfg`, passive segment + memory.init, split across segments, built by i32.store immediates, UTF-16 (AssemblyScript), memory64 module\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Natural Mastery/next-day twist of D16. Fixtures via wat2wasm: (a) custom section named hcf\n  {\"id\": \"bytecode-containers\", \"concept\": \"LLVM bitcode, Python .pyc, Lua luac, standalone .class/.dex as group members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixtures: clang-18 -c -emit-llvm (BC C0 DE + wrapper), python -m py_compile (3.x magic), luac (installed), javac single class. Record magic -> candidate format labels (`llvm_bitcode`/`bitcode`, `pyc`, `\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-singlefile-aot\", \"concept\": \".NET single-file bundle, ReadyToRun and NativeAOT builds\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). dotnet installed: `dotnet publish -p:PublishSingleFile=true` (apphost + bundle manifest, `.net core bundle` signature hash), `-p:PublishReadyToRun=true` (R2R header in CLI dll), `-p:PublishAot=true` (native ELF, no ...\"}\n  {\"id\": \"upx-packed-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"UPX-packed ELF/PE (plain and with scrubbed UPX! magic / renamed sections)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixture: `upx -9` a C ELF + MinGW PE carrying an HCFG `.hcfg` section; variant with `UPX!` zeroed and UPX0/1 renamed. Target: solver detects (packer_info), restores magic, `upx -d` on a copy, then hcfg_find + \n  {\"id\": \"aes-tea-chacha-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"HCFG encrypted with AES-128/256 (ECB/CBC/CTR), XTEA, ChaCha20\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixture style of TARGETS.json: key/IV as adjacent 16/32-byte raw or printable strings, or derived (sha256 of campaign-like string). Extractor: locate cipher by constants (S-box 637c777b, 0x9e3779b9, 'expand 32-byte k'\n  {\"id\": \"stack-built-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"HCFG assembled at runtime from mov-immediate stores / per-char pushes\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixture: gcc -O0/-O2 C that writes the blob via volatile stack stores (x86-64 and AArch64). Extractor: capstone imm collection per function in store order, fallback unicorn emulation of the builder (no syscalls),\n  {\"id\": \"multiarch-machine-labels\", \"concept\": \"ELF/PE/Mach-O machine words for i386, ARM, AArch64, MIPS(el), PPC/PPC64, RISC-V, SPARC + big-endian HCFG ints\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). lib/knowledge.py ELF_MACHINE has only 4 entries. Fixtures: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc (linkable) and clang-18 --target=<arch> -c (ET_REL .o; no lld installed) each with \n  {\"id\": \"macho-hcfg-section\", \"concept\": \"Mach-O thin + fat universal binary with HCFG in a `__DATA,__hcfg` section\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). clang-18 --target=x86_64-apple-macos -c and arm64-apple-macos -c produce MH_OBJECT files (no ld64); hand-pack a FAT header with python for the universal case. Targets: format label (`macho` presumed), machi\n  {\"id\": \"resource-overlay-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"HCFG in PE RT_RCDATA, .NET manifest resource, jar non-class entry, or file overlay\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"pr