{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Awxx9twUFuHfZ6RTYrHV8A","type":"tool_result","content":"186:| hcfg_version / xor_key_hex | header byte 4 decimal / header byte 5 as `0x%02x` | — |\n187:| has_hcfg_section (enum) | `true` when a section is literally named `.hcfg` | — |\n188:| hcfg_offset (integer) | decimal FILE offset: base64 text start (`S`), RAW = the `HCFG` magic | — |\n189:| hcfg_storage (enum, D17 revised contract; re-confirmed D18 single/TT/Mastery) | `base64` (SENGR literal), `raw_hcfg_section` (in a `.hcfg` section), `raw_const_array` (other native data section, e.g. FPC `.data`), `wasm_data_segment`, `raw` (else) | every free-text spelling for raw-stored (raw, raw_data, section, .hcfg, bytes, blob, ... ~10.9k probes) -- the token set is closed |\n190:| compression_methods (jar, json) | sorted distinct ZIP method ids, compact: `[0,8]` (D17 text: Stored/Deflate names, any order also accepted) | — |\n191:Naming law (from playbook.py): native format = container only; a managed .NET binary = container_runtime (pe+cli).\n192:Java broke the compound law (`jar`), so when a label is new, try the plain container name AND the compound, one per POST.\n193:\n194:## Pitfalls that cost time\n195:- **A synthetic label with no derivable spelling** (D3 .NET format ~1.5 h; D17 raw `hcfg_storage`, ~10.9k POSTs over 3.5 h,\n196:  NEVER guessed -- solved only by the organizers' contract revision to an enum): stop after ~10 single-id probes plus one `hctf\n197:  labels` run, write HELP.md, then RE-PULL THE CONTRACT periodically and diff each id's question/answer_format. Never put the\n198:  unknown id into a batch with other open ids; mass automated grouptests on an exact_text label are wasted POSTs.\n199:- **A re-asked field must inherit its family's absence rule** (D17 TT/Mastery): new `recover_code` code fell back to a leaf\n200:  heuristic on a stripped d01 although `disassembly` had learnt `[]` on D8. Absent symbol => `none`/`[]`/`false`, always.\n201:- **A multi-field POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the set and hides which field was wrong (D2). Submit\n202:  unconfirmed/new fields ALONE; batch only the known ones (D17: 10 new derivable fields in one POST was fine -- all bytes-derived).\n203:- **Chasing the prompt's theme** (D5-D18): the NEW day's flavour has never been asked (D18's call graph / \"prove no injection\"\n204:  included); read the contract ids first. But keep the facts you learn about each language/theme: a later backfill re-asks old\n205:  days' facts (D17 re-asked D1/D2/D4-D7), so record the theme facts in NOTES.md for the backfill day.\n206:- **Shell/JSON quoting** of `Global\\Huntress...` mutexes: build the submit JSON with python/jq, not by hand in a shell string.\n207:- **capstone `ret` has an empty op_str**: `f\"{m} {o}\"` gives `\"ret \"`. Strip it, and convert immediates to decimal.\n208:- **Cumulative zip**: old groups' answers carry over when their sha256 match; POST the known ids first (they bank as\n209:  `accepted`), then the new/unknown ids alone (D15: 140 banked at T+17 s; D17: 188 at T+18 s).\n210:- **A new id shape on an old field** (D15 `analysis_stripped_machine`): peel a member qualifier off the front before declaring\n211:  the field unknown; never answer it from the \"first\" member of the group.\n212:- **Recursive unzip** destroys nested containers (.jar/.apk) and their `dNN--` prefix; keep them whole.\n213:- **Same field name, different `kind`** (D8 elf_class/machine): read `answer_format.kind` per id.\n214:- **Huge members** (D8: 67 MB Swift): no per-key xor brute force or per-field re-parse; cheap encodings first, crc-gate every hit,\n215:  parse each member once.\n216:- **Decoy magics** (D9 Nim): code that CHECKS the magic embeds `\"HCFG\"` literals; len 0 => crc32(b\"\")==0 passes! Require non-empty\n217:  JSON that parses, keep scanning, then try the base64 form.\n218:- **Location fields per scan path** (D12): a decoder with raw AND base64 branches must return the hit offset (and, since D17, the\n219:  hit's encoding for `hcfg_storage`) from BOTH. Assert no `none` where a config was decoded.\n220:- **`strings -t d` offsets on Nim/Swift literals** can be off by 1: use `grep -abo` / `re.finditer(...).start()`.\n221:- **Jar members are deflated**: `grep HCFG file.jar` finds nothing. Inflate the class, read constant-pool strings.\n222:- **Stripped builds / renamed functions** in variants (D1 TT, D2 Mastery set2, D8/D15/D16 Mastery d01): answer what the question\n223:  defines for absence (`[]`, `none`, `false`); never substitute a heuristic constant.\n224:- **Tool parity**: ilspycmd, dotnet, rustfilt, GoReSym, rabin2, swift-demangle are in `bin/`; monodis/de4dot/gnat are not.\n225:- **Timed windows**: download dominates (D16 TT 52 s of 64 s on the 32 MB bundle). After editing hctf/*.py, restart the\n226:  orchestrator (D1/D2 ran stale modules).\n227:- **WASM parsing**: section sizes are 5-byte PADDED LEB128; read LEB128 generically (`lib.binary.wasm_layout`).\n228:- **PE machine map must include 0x8664 → `x86-64`**: a from-scratch replay once emitted `0x8664` and failed TT twice.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c90f1-c3ad-4e71-909e-30857e8a1663","uuid":"f91fb730-393c-4616-ae64-291aea78a88f","timestamp":"2026-10-18T13:04:41.021Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"186:| hcfg_version / xor_key_hex | header byte 4 decimal / header byte 5 as `0x%02x` | — |\n187:| has_hcfg_section (enum) | `true` when a section is literally named `.hcfg` | — |\n188:| hcfg_offset (integer) | decimal FILE offset: base64 text start (`S`), RAW = the `HCFG` magic | — |\n189:| hcfg_storage (enum, D17 revised contract; re-confirmed D18 single/TT/Mastery) | `base64` (SENGR literal), `raw_hcfg_section` (in a `.hcfg` section), `raw_const_array` (other native data section, e.g. FPC `.data`), `wasm_data_segment`, `raw` (else) | every free-text spelling for raw-stored (raw, raw_data, section, .hcfg, bytes, blo