{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9kauh6eWFrRFk36SKTH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HddoyY2TXtPaNffgvfmKzL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\nt=open(p).read()\nm=re.search(r'(## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n)(.*?)(```)',t,re.S)\ng=json.loads(m.group(2))\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='fortran-gfortran-member']\nby={x['id']:x for x in g}\nfor k in ['hcfg-storage-classifier','question-rule-extractor','offset-section-mapper','ada-gnat-deep-facts']:\n    x=by[k]; x['priority']=2\n    if not x['detail'].startswith('BUILT'): x['detail']='BUILT (prebuild-state ok). '+x['detail']\nby['elf-header-segment-facts']['priority']=2\nby['elf-header-segment-facts']['detail']='NOT BUILT (1st attempt killed rc -9, nothing written: keep the scope small -- pyelftools only, no Ghidra). '+by['elf-header-segment-facts']['detail']\nx=by['new-language-fingerprints']\nx['concept']='Haskell, OCaml, V, Odin, COBOL, Modula-2, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka (Ada seen D17, Fortran seen D18)'\nD='challenges/day18/binary-flow-state'\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"theme-facts-recording\",\"concept\":\"Record each day's (unasked) prompt-theme facts during the single solve so the later backfill answers without re-analysis\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names.\"},\n {\"id\":\"fortran-gfortran-deep-facts\",\"concept\":\"gfortran facts for the d18 group when its theme is backfilled: source file name, MAIN__, internal procedures (name.N), select_string case table, libgfortran imports, .comment GCC banner\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Fixtures: copy the cached d18 members (single variant-000 + TT/Mastery variants under \"+D+\"/solver/cases/*/artifacts) into tests/data/binary_fixtures (gfortran compiler is NOT installed; runtime libgfortran.so.5 is). Facts: source_file `variant-000.f90` (STT_FILE), main_program `MAIN__`, procedures [event_failure, event_sandbox, event_decoy, event_success] with and without the `.N` suffix (table order + address order), case table = `_gfortran_select_string` struct array {low_ptr, low_len, high_ptr, high_len, case_no} x N (entry 0 = default, NULL ptrs) -> [(case_string, case_no)] e.g. analysis->1, sandbox->2, workstation->3, env var `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (the edi string passed to _gfortran_get_environment_variable_i4), imports list (9 `_gfortran_*`), NEEDED [libgfortran.so.5, libm.so.6, libgcc_s.so.1, libc.so.6], hcfg symbol `encoded_config.4`. Expose all as facts-dict keys with plain names (procedures, case_values, env_var, needed, imports, source_file).\"},\n {\"id\":\"callgraph-indirect-flow-facts\",\"concept\":\"Generic call graph with indirect-call resolution for ELF/PE: per-function callees, PLT import edges, `mov/lea reg, imm; call reg` targets, call-table/jump-table targets, entry->main chain\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 prompt: 'Reconstruct the call graph ... follow the calls' (unasked). Implement lib.binary.call_graph(data) with capstone linear sweep over FUNC symbols (fallback: .eh_frame FDE ranges / rizin `aaa;aflj` when stripped): direct `call rel32` -> callee symbol or PLT import name (resolve via .rela.plt), `call reg` resolved by backward scan for `mov e/rax, imm32` or `lea rax, [rip+x]` in the same block, `call [rip+x]` via GOT/data pointer. Output edges [[caller, callee, kind(direct|plt|indirect)]] in address order, plus indirect_call_count, indirect_targets, functions_reached_from(main). Fixtures: d18 Fortran (4 indirect `call rax` to event_*), d01 C, d15 stripped/symbolized pair, a PE (d02 MinGW). Candidate GM shapes: JSON array of callee names, integer counts, `none` when stripped.\"},\n {\"id\":\"api-intent-injection-classifier\",\"concept\":\"Classify each imported/called API by intent and give an injection verdict (ELF + PE), mapping to MITRE T1055.x\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 prompt: 'read the API intent at each edge, and prove no injection hides in the flow'; trace effects `modeled_process_access_no_injection`. Table (lib/knowledge.py-style dict, not lib edits by workers): env_query (getenv, _gfortran_get_environment_variable_i4, GetEnvironmentVariable), output (printf/puts/write/_gfortran_st_write*), string (strcmp/_gfortran_select_string/string_len_trim), process_access (ptrace ATTACH/PEEK, OpenProcess, /proc/<pid>/mem read), injection (ptrace POKETEXT/POKEDATA/SETREGS, process_vm_writev, VirtualAllocEx+WriteProcessMemory+CreateRemoteThread, NtMapViewOfSection, QueueUserAPC, SetWindowsHookEx, SetThreadContext, LD_PRELOAD/dlopen of a written file, memfd_create+execve), network (socket/connect/WSAStartup/WinHttp*). Facts: api_intents {name: intent}, has_injection (true/false), injection_apis [] , process_access_apis. Fixtures: d18 (no injection), plus small gcc/MinGW-free fixtures that import process_vm_writev / ptrace (PE: build import table with pefile or use existing PE fixtures).\"},\n {\"id\":\"dynamic-trace-template-facts\",\"concept\":\"Parse the `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` trace template embedded in every member (D2-D18) and model its env-gated branches\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Every member carries a format template like `{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"<b>\\\",\\\"event_count\\\":<n>,\\\"campaign\\\":\\\"BRNN-00V\\\",\\\"family\\\":\\\"fortran_indirect_flow_trace\\\",\\\"effects\\\":\\\"modeled_process_access_no_injection\\\",\\\"network\\\":\\\"none\\\"}` (jar: constant-pool strings; wasm: data segment; some keys filled at runtime: manifest_entries, archive_score, selector `eventCountForModel:` on ObjC). Families seen: d10 non_mutating_service_plan, d11 synthetic_document_manifest, d12 private_scratch_archive_manifest, d14 non_mutating_trigger_plan, d15 symbol_loss_equivalent_trace, d17 ada_encoded_config_trace, d18 fortran_indirect_flow_trace. Extract per member: schema, family, effects, network, static key list, host-model options (`analysis`/`sandbox`/`workstation`), env var name (`HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`), and the branch/event chosen per option (static from the case table / compare chain; optional sandboxed run under bwrap with --unshare-net and the env set, ELF x86-64 only, never on the host). Facts keys: trace_schema, trace_family, trace_effects, trace_network, host_model_env, host_models, branch_for_<model>.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jumptable-switch-recovery\",\"concept\":\"Recover switch/SELECT CASE dispatch: gcc relative int32 tables (`movsxd rax,[rdx+rax*4]; add rax,rdx; jmp rax`), absolute 8-byte tables, MSVC/MinGW tables, gfortran select_string case arrays, Go/Rust match tables\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 dispatched on `_gfortran_select_string` + cmp chain; a stripped or -O2 sequel uses a real jump table. Implement lib.binary.switch_tables(data): find `jmp reg` preceded by a bounded index (cmp/ja) and a table base (lea rip+x), read N entries, map case -> target address -> symbol. Fixtures: clang-18/gcc -O2 C switch with 6+ dense cases (ELF + `-static`), the d18 case table, an AArch64 `br x` table (aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc). Output: [{case, target, symbol}] and case_count.\"},\n {\"id\":\"anti-analysis-gating-facts\",\"concept\":\"Anti-analysis / sandbox gating facts: environment and host-model checks, decoy branches, debugger/VM detection (TracerPid, ptrace TRACEME, CPUID hypervisor bit, DMI/VM vendor strings, rdtsc timing)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 had event_sandbox/event_decoy branches selected by HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL -- an 'evasion' theme is a natural next day. Facts: anti_debug (bool + technique list: ptrace_traceme, tracerpid, isdebuggerpresent, ntqueryinformationprocess, timing), anti_vm (cpuid_hypervisor, vm_strings list), env_gates [env var names compared], decoy_functions (symbols named *decoy*, or branches that skip the HCFG). MITRE T1497 / T1622. Fixtures: small gcc C ELFs with each check (static analysis only; never execute).\"},\n {\"id\":\"flattened-dispatcher-recovery\",\"concept\":\"Control-flow flattening (OLLVM-style state-variable dispatcher) and opaque predicates: recover the original block order / state transitions\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Title pun 'Flow State' -> state machine; OLLVM is not installed, so hand-write fixtures: C with `switch(state)` inside `while(1)` where each case sets the next state (constants xor'd), plus opaque predicates `x*(x+1)%2==0`. Extractor: identify the dispatcher (block with most predecessors + cmp/jmp on one stack var), emulate each case with unicorn to read the next-state constant, output the state sequence [s0, s1, ...], the executed block order, and the final return value (ties into emulate-return-value). Fixtures in ELF x86-64 and one MinGW-free PE via existing PE fixture style.\"},\n {\"id\":\"gcc-frontend-modula2-member\",\"concept\":\"Next GCC front-end languages as a new-day member: Modula-2 (gm2), COBOL (gcobol, GCC 15), Algol 68 (ga68), gccgo\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D17 Ada and D18 Fortran were consecutive GCC front-ends (dynamic glibc, HCFG RAW in .rodata, carried-over solver answered both). Cues: gm2 NEEDED libm2pim.so.20/libm2iso.so.20/libm2rts, symbols `_M2_<Module>_init`/`_M2_<Module>_fini`/`_M2_<Module>_ctor`, `M2RTS_`; gcobol NEEDED libgcobol.so, `__gg__` symbols; gccgo NEEDED libgo.so.23, `__go_`/`main.main` symbols, `.go_export` section, NO `.go.buildinfo`; ga68 `libga68`. Install check: `apt-cache policy gm2 gfortran gccgo gcobol` -- build fixtures with an HCFG raw .rodata const array; confirm format elf / x86-64 and that hcfg_find + language_of return sane tokens (add the cue strings to language_of).\"},\n {\"id\":\"direct-syscall-facts\",\"concept\":\"APIs invoked by raw `syscall` instructions instead of imports (static/no-libc binaries): syscall numbers -> names -> intent\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"An 'API intent' / 'prove no injection' sequel can hide process_vm_writev (310), ptrace (101), memfd_create (319), execve (59) behind inline syscalls. Extractor: capstone scan for `syscall` (x86-64) / `svc #0` (AArch64) / `int 0x80` (i386), backward-resolve the eax/x8 immediate, map with the x86-64/aarch64/i386 syscall tables (embed as dicts), feed api-intent-injection-classifier. Fixtures: gcc -nostdlib -static C with inline asm syscalls.\"},\n {\"id\":\"lisp-scheme-member\",\"concept\":\"Lisp-family native images as a new-day member: SBCL core-embedded executable, Chicken Scheme (csc), Racket `raco exe`, ECL\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Remaining 'unusual runtime' languages after Haskell/OCaml/Fortran. Cues: SBCL huge static ELF with `SBCL` + core appended (`\\\\x00\\\\x00\\\\x00\\\\x00CORE` magic / `--core` strings, `sb-impl::`), Chicken `C_toplevel`, `libchicken.so.11`, `C_` symbols, Racket `.rackboot` section / `racket/base` strings, ECL `libecl.so`. HCFG likely a string literal (raw or base64) inside a heap image: raw/base64 scan must still work; offsets = first stored byte. Build fixtures only if the compilers are apt-installable (`apt-cache policy sbcl chicken-bin racket ecl`).\"},\n]\ng=g+new\n# order: priority then keep relative\ng.sort(key=lambda x:x['priority'])\nbody='[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+'\\n]\\n'\njson.loads(body)\nt=t[:m.start(2)]+body+t[m.end(2):]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\nt=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md').read()\ng=json.loads(re.search(r'## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n(.*?)```',t,re.S).group(1))\ns=json.load(open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (lambda st: st and (st.get('ok') or st.get('attempts',0)>=2))(s.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+x['id']))]\nprint(len(g),len(pend),pend)\nprint(all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g), len({x['id'] for x in g})==len(g))\nEOF\nwc -l /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":849,"cache_read_input_tokens":125758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":849},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c90f1-c3ad-4e71-909e-30857e8a1663","uuid":"3dae389d-b542-44b4-a3ea-12fce18272e2","timestamp":"2026-10-18T13:07:12.262Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9kauLWs7cipQa2svyGc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HddoyY2TXtPaNffgvfmKzL":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\nt=open(p).read()\nm=re.search(r'(## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n)(.*?)(```)',t,re.S)\ng=json.loads(m.group(2))\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='fortran-gfortran-member']\nby={x['id']:x for x in g}\nfor k in ['hcfg-storage-classifier','question-rule-extractor','offset-section-mapper','ada-gnat-deep-facts']:\n    x=by[k]; x['priority']=2\n    if not x['detail'].startswith('BUILT'): x['detail']='BUILT (prebuild-state ok). '+x['detail']\nby['elf-header-segment-facts']['priority']=2\nby['elf-header-segment-facts']['detail']='NOT BUILT (1st attempt killed rc -9, nothing written: keep the scope small -- pyelftools only, no Ghidra). '+by['elf-header-segment-facts']['detail']\nx=by['new-language-fingerprints']\nx['concept']='Haskell, OCaml, V, Odin, COBOL, Modula-2, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka (Ada seen D17, Fortran seen D18)'\nD='challenges/day18/binary-flow-state'\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"theme-facts-recording\",\"concept\":\"Record each day's (unasked) prompt-theme facts during the single solve so the later backfill answers without re-analysis\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names.\"},\n {\"id\":\"fortran-gfortran-deep-facts\",\"concept\":\"gfortran facts for the d18 group when its theme is backfilled: source file name, MAIN__, internal procedures (name.N), select_string case table, libgfortran imports, .comment GCC banner\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Fixtures: copy the cached d18 members (single variant-000 + TT/Mastery variants under \"+D+\"/solver/cases/*/artifacts) into tests/data/binary_fixtures (gfortran compiler is NOT installed; runtime libgfortran.so.5 is). Facts: source_file `variant-000.f90` (STT_FILE), main_program `MAIN__`, procedures [event_failure, event_sandbox, event_decoy, event_success] with and without the `.N` suffix (table order + address order), case table = `_gfortran_select_string` struct array {low_ptr, low_len, high_ptr, high_len, case_no} x N (entry 0 = default, NULL ptrs) -> [(case_string, case_no)] e.g. analysis->1, sandbox->2, workstation->3, env var `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (the edi string passed to _gfortran_get_environment_variable_i4), imports list (9 `_gfortran_*`), NEEDED [libgfortran.so.5, libm.so.6, libgcc_s.so.1, libc.so.6], hcfg symbol `encoded_config.4`. Expose all as facts-dict keys with plain names (procedures, case_values, env_var, needed, imports, source_file).\"},\n {\"id\":\"callgraph-indirect-flow-facts\",\"concept\":\"Generic call graph with indirect-call resolution for ELF/PE: per-function callees, PLT import edges, `mov/lea reg, imm; call reg` targets, call-table/jump-table targets, entry->main chain\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 prompt: 'Reconstruct the call graph ... follow the calls' (unasked). Implement lib.binary.call_graph(data) with capstone linear sweep over FUNC symbols (fallback: .eh_frame FDE ranges / rizin `aaa;aflj` when stripped): direct `call rel32` -> callee symbol or PLT import name (resolve via .rela.plt), `call reg` resolved by backward scan for `mov e/rax, imm32` or `lea rax, [rip+x]` in the same block, `call [rip+x]` via GOT/data pointer. Output edges [[caller, callee, kind(direct|plt|indirect)]] in address order, plus indirect_call_count, indirect_targets, functions_reached_from(main). Fixtures: d18 Fortran (4 indirect `call rax` to event_*), d01 C, d15 stripped/symbolized pair, a PE (d02 MinGW). Candidate GM shapes: JSON array of callee names, integer counts, `none` when stripped.\"},\n {\"id\":\"api-intent-injection-classifier\",\"concept\":\"Classify each imported/called API by intent and give an injection verdict (ELF + PE), mapping to MITRE T1055.x\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 prompt: 'read the API intent at each edge, and prove no injection hides in the flow'; trace effects `modeled_process_access_no_injection`. Table (lib/knowledge.py-style dict, not lib edits by workers): env_query (getenv, _gfortran_get_environment_variable_i4, GetEnvironmentVariable), output (printf/puts/write/_gfortran_st_write*), string (strcmp/_gfortran_select_string/string_len_trim), process_access (ptrace ATTACH/PEEK, OpenProcess, /proc/<pid>/mem read), injection (ptrace POKETEXT/POKEDATA/SETREGS, process_vm_writev, VirtualAllocEx+WriteProcessMemory+CreateRemoteThread, NtMapViewOfSection, QueueUserAPC, SetWindowsHookEx, SetThreadContext, LD_PRELOAD/dlopen of a written file, memfd_create+execve), network (socket/connect/WSAStartup/WinHttp*). Facts: api_intents {name: intent}, has_injection (true/false), injection_apis [] , process_access_apis. Fixtures: d18 (no injection), plus small gcc/MinGW-free fixtures that import process_vm_writev / ptrace (PE: build import table with pefile or use existing PE fixtures).\"},\n {\"id\":\"dynamic-trace-template-facts\",\"concept\":\"Parse the `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` trace template embedded in every member (D2-D18) and model its env-gated branches\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Every member carries a format template like `{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"<b>\\\",\\\"event_count\\\":<n>,\\\"campaign\\\":\\\"BRNN-00V\\\",\\\"family\\\":\\\"fortran_indirect_flow_trace\\\",\\\"effects\\\":\\\"modeled_process_access_no_injection\\\",\\\"network\\\":\\\"none\\\"}` (jar: constant-pool strings; wasm: data segment; some keys filled at runtime: manifest_entries, archive_score, selector `eventCountForModel:` on ObjC). Families seen: d10 non_mutating_service_plan, d11 synthetic_document_manifest, d12 private_scratch_archive_manifest, d14 non_mutating_trigger_plan, d15 symbol_loss_equivalent_trace, d17 ada_encoded_config_trace, d18 fortran_indirect_flow_trace. Extract per member: schema, family, effects, network, static key list, host-model options (`analysis`/`sandbox`/`workstation`), env var name (`HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`), and the branch/event chosen per option (static from the case table / compare chain; optional sandboxed run under bwrap with --unshare-net and the env set, ELF x86-64 only, never on the host). Facts keys: trace_schema, trace_family, trace_effects, trace_network, host_model_env, host_models, branch_for_<model>.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jumptable-switch-recovery\",\"concept\":\"Recover switch/SELECT CASE dispatch: gcc relative int32 tables (`movsxd rax,[rdx+rax*4]; add rax,rdx; jmp rax`), absolute 8-byte tables, MSVC/MinGW tables, gfortran select_string case arrays, Go/Rust match tables\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 dispatched on `_gfortran_select_string` + cmp chain; a stripped or -O2 sequel uses a real jump table. Implement lib.binary.switch_tables(data): find `jmp reg` preceded by a bounded index (cmp/ja) and a table base (lea rip+x), read N entries, map case -> target address -> symbol. Fixtures: clang-18/gcc -O2 C switch with 6+ dense cases (ELF + `-static`), the d18 case table, an AArch64 `br x` table (aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc). Output: [{case, target, symbol}] and case_count.\"},\n {\"id\":\"anti-analysis-gating-facts\",\"concept\":\"Anti-analysis / sandbox gating facts: environment and host-model checks, decoy branches, debugger/VM detection (TracerPid, ptrace TRACEME, CPUID hypervisor bit, DMI/VM vendor strings, rdtsc timing)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 had event_sandbox/event_decoy branches selected by HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL -- an 'evasion' theme is a natural next day. Facts: anti_debug (bool + technique list: ptrace_traceme, tracerpid, isdebuggerpresent, ntqueryinformationprocess, timing), anti_vm (cpuid_hypervisor, vm_strings list), env_gates [env var names compared], decoy_functions (symbols named *decoy*, or branches that skip the HCFG). MITRE T1497 / T1622. Fixtures: small gcc C ELFs with each check (static analysis only; never execute).\"},\n {\"id\":\"flattened-dispatcher-recovery\",\"concept\":\"Control-flow flattening (OLLVM-style state-variable dispatcher) and opaque predicates: recover the original block order / state transitions\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Title pun 'Flow State' -> state machine; OLLVM is not installed, so hand-write fixtures: C with `switch(state)` inside `while(1)` where each case sets the next state (constants xor'd), plus opaque predicates `x*(x+1)%2==0`. Extractor: identify the dispatcher (block with most predecessors + cmp/jmp on one stack var), emulate each case with unicorn to read the next-state constant, output the state sequence [s0, s1, ...], the executed block order, and the final return value (ties into emulate-return-value). Fixtures in ELF x86-64 and one MinGW-free PE via existing PE fixture style.\"},\n {\"id\":\"gcc-frontend-modula2-member\",\"concept\":\"Next GCC front-end languages as a new-day member: Modula-2 (gm2), COBOL (gcobol, GCC 15), Algol 68 (ga68), gccgo\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D17 Ada and D18 Fortran were consecutive GCC front-ends (dynamic glibc, HCFG RAW in .rodata, carried-over solver answered both). Cues: gm2 NEEDED libm2pim.so.20/libm2iso.so.20/libm2rts, symbols `_M2_<Module>_init`/`_M2_<Module>_fini`/`_M2_<Module>_ctor`, `M2RTS_`; gcobol NEEDED libgcobol.so, `__gg__` symbols; gccgo NEEDED libgo.so.23, `__go_`/`main.main` symbols, `.go_export` section, NO `.go.buildinfo`; ga68 `libga68`. Install check: `apt-cache policy gm2 gfortran gccgo gcobol` -- build fixtures with an HCFG raw .rodata const array; confirm format elf / x86-64 and that hcfg_find + language_of return sane tokens (add the cue strings to language_of).\"},\n {\"id\":\"direct-syscall-facts\",\"concept\":\"APIs invoked by raw `syscall` instructions instead of imports (static/no-libc binaries): syscall numbers -> names -> intent\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"An 'API intent' / 'prove no injection' sequel can hide process_vm_writev (310), ptrace (101), memfd_create (319), execve (59) behind inline syscalls. Extractor: capstone scan for `syscall` (x86-64) / `svc #0` (AArch64) / `int 0x80` (i386), backward-resolve the eax/x8 immediate, map with the x86-64/aarch64/i386 syscall tables (embed as dicts), feed api-intent-injection-classifier. Fixtures: gcc -nostdlib -static C with inline asm syscalls.\"},\n {\"id\":\"lisp-scheme-member\",\"concept\":\"Lisp-family native images as a new-day member: SBCL core-embedded executable, Chicken Scheme (csc), Racket `raco exe`, ECL\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Remaining 'unusual runtime' languages after Haskell/OCaml/Fortran. Cues: SBCL huge static ELF with `SBCL` + core appended (`\\\\x00\\\\x00\\\\x00\\\\x00CORE` magic / `--core` strings, `sb-impl::`), Chicken `C_toplevel`, `libchicken.so.11`, `C_` symbols, Racket `.rackboot` section / `racket/base` strings, ECL `libecl.so`. HCFG likely a string literal (raw or base64) inside a heap image: raw/base64 scan must still work; offsets = first stored byte. Build fixtures only if the compilers are apt-installable (`apt-cache policy sbcl chicken-bin racket ecl`).\"},\n]\ng=g+new\n# order: priority then keep relative\ng.sort(key=lambda x:x['priority'])\nbody='[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+'\\n]\\n'\njson.loads(body)\nt=t[:m.start(2)]+body+t[m.end(2):]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\nt=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md').read()\ng=json.loads(re.search(r'## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n(.*?)```',t,re.S).group(1))\ns=json.load(open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (lambda st: st and (st.get('ok') or st.get('attempts',0)>=2))(s.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+x['id']))]\nprint(len(g),len(pend),pend)\nprint(all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g), len({x['id'] for x in g})==len(g))\nEOF\nwc -l /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md"}}}
