{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PKjMDiPS5LvcQ5FwJmXWCp","type":"tool_result","content":"Progression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\nlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix from the file-name tag (C ELF\n`stripped`/`symbolized`; WebAssembly `compact`/`direct`, labels `wasm`/`wasm32`); D17 \"Decoder Ring\" = back to ONE new language\n(Ada/GNAT ELF, HCFG RAW in `.rodata`, nothing new to decode) + BACKFILL #2 (160 -> 204 ids, 11 per old group) that re-asked\nEARLIER DAYS' single-solve facts (d01 marker/recover_code, d02 mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol, d04 has_go_runtime, d05\nhas_rust_mangled_symbol, d06 methods/access_flags, d07 method_count/has_coroutine_runtime) and a NEW label field `hcfg_storage`\n(an ENUM after the organizers' mid-day contract revision: base64 / raw_hcfg_section / raw_const_array / wasm_data_segment / raw,\npicked by an ordered rule list in the question text; before the revision ~10.9k free-text probes failed). TT/Mastery: d01 re-rolled\nSTRIPPED -> `recover_code` `none`. **D18 \"Flow State\"** = ONE Fortran (gfortran) ELF, exactly as forecast (prebuild\n`fortran-gfortran-member`): HCFG RAW in `.rodata` (`encoded_config.4`, offset 8512 in every variant), 216 ids = 204 + 12 new-group\nids, NO backfill, CORRECT at T+11 s from the carried-over solver; TT/Mastery (4 sets) first try, d01 NOT stripped this time. The\nD18 theme (\"reconstruct the call graph, read the API intent at each edge, prove no injection\") was unasked; the binary's flow =\ngetenv(`HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`) -> `_gfortran_select_string` case table -> indirect `call rax` to `event_{decoy,sandbox,failure,\nsuccess}` -> trace JSON (`fortran_indirect_flow_trace`, effects `modeled_process_access_no_injection`). Every member since D2\nembeds such a `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` template -- a backfill can ask branch/event/family/effects facts. Lessons for D19+: (a) the next backfill will most likely\nreach D8-D17's own day facts (Swift/Nim/Zig/D/FPC/Crystal/ObjC/pair/wasm/Ada identity booleans, symbol names, class/selector\nlists, wasm imports/exports) -- the \"theme\" of a day is answerable LATER on its old group; (b) the new-day member keeps being a\nplain ELF whose ids the carried-over solver already answers (D17 group banked at T+18 s); (c) label fields with no derivable\nspelling (`hcfg_storage` raw, D3 `pe_cli`) are the real time sink -- and the organizers fix them by REVISING THE CONTRACT\n(enum + rule text), so re-pull it instead of guessing; (d) location/storage-classification fields (`hcfg_offset`,\n`hcfg_storage`) need offset -> section/segment mapping on every container. Asked field names: config_*, format, machine, architecture,\nelf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols, section_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*,\nhas_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags,\nmethod_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset, hcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods.\nRemaining risks: (1) more per-language fact backfills, (2) a twist that hides the HCFG from a byte scan (the D17 \"decoder\" theme\ndid not materialise but stays plausible: packing, real crypto, stack-built, per-string encryption, API hashing), (3) a new\ncontainer/arch label (Mach-O, eBPF, AArch64...), (4) more pair days with `_`-containing tags.\n\nTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\n reference/KPI.md                                   |   1 +\n reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md   |  67 +++++--\n reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md           |  40 ++--\n reference/coverage/mobile-android.md               |  53 +++--\n reference/coverage/script-analysis.md              |  76 +++++---\n reference/coverage/warmups.md                      |  86 +++++----\n reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md | 103 +++++-----\n reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md         | 213 ++++++++++-----------\n reference/techniques/mobile-android.md             | 109 ++++++-----\n reference/techniques/script-analysis.md            | 131 +++++++------\n reference/techniques/warmups.md                    |  68 ++++---\n 11 files changed, 544 insertions(+), 403 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c90f1-c3ad-4e71-909e-30857e8a1663","uuid":"871b857b-28f6-44be-84b3-8158dfa753c5","timestamp":"2026-10-18T13:07:16.533Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Progression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\nlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix from the file-name tag (C ELF\n`stripped`/`symbolized`; WebAssembly `compact`/`direct`, labels `wasm`/`wasm32`); D17 \"Decoder Ring\" = back to ONE new language\n(Ada/GNAT ELF, HCFG RAW in `.rodata`, nothing new to decode) + BACKFILL #2 (160 -> 204 ids, 11 per old group) that re-asked\nEARLIER DAYS' single-solve facts (d01 marker/recover_code, d02 mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol, d04 has_go_runtime, d05\nhas_rust_mangled_symbol, d06 methods/access_flags, d07 method_count/has_coroutine_runtime) and a NEW label field `hcfg_storage`\n(an ENUM after the organizers' mid-day contract revision: base64 / raw_hcfg_section / raw_const_array / wasm_data_segment / raw,\npicked by an ordered rule list in the question text; before the revision ~10.9k free-text probes failed). TT/Mastery: d01 re-rolled\nSTRIPPED -> `recover_code` `none`. **D18 \"Flow State\"** = ONE Fortran (gfortran) ELF, exactly as forecast (prebuild\n`fortran-gfortran-member`): HCFG RAW in `.rodata` (`encoded_config.4`, offset 8512 in every variant), 216 ids = 204 + 12 new-group\nids, NO backfill, CO