{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9kgETbTf1MH6NfVCY69","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've updated both files: the technique log and the coverage atlas for the binary lane. Day 18 was solved first try in every mode (single-solve correct at 11 seconds after start, Time Trial in 8 s, Mastery in 14 s). No tests were run and no game modes were touched.\n\n1. **`reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md`**: added the day 18 \"Flow State\" entry. The new member was a small Fortran program. Its config blob sat unencrypted in the read-only data section, at offset 8512 in every variant. The old solver answered all 216 questions with no new code. I recorded the program's flow and how to recognise it, and noted that the prompt's theme (call graph, \"prove no injection\") again wasn't asked. I also recorded that every member since day 2 embeds an unasked \"dynamic trace\" template keyed on the `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` environment variable, which a later backfill could ask about. New variant axes: same offset across variants, d01 not stripped this time, 4 Mastery sets. I shortened day 17 and merged the pitfalls, but the file is 224 lines, a bit over the ~200 target.\n2. **`reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md`**: marked Fortran `seen D18` (yesterday's forecast was right) and added four concept rows: call graph and indirect calls, API intent and injection verdict, the trace template, and anti-analysis gating. The recognition-cues section is 48 lines (limit 60) and gained Fortran and theme-fact lines. I removed the Fortran gap and lowered the priority of four gaps that have already been built.\n3. **Prebuild queue**: it now holds 11 unbuilt gaps (the minimum is 8), all with new ids, and the JSON is valid. The top-priority ones target the most likely backfill of today's theme: deeper Fortran facts, call-graph reconstruction, an API-intent/injection classifier, and parsing the trace templates. Then come jump-table/switch recovery, anti-analysis facts, flattened-dispatcher recovery and other GCC-compiled languages (Modula-2, COBOL), plus raw-syscall detection and Lisp-family members. The leftover `elf-header-segment-facts` gap is still unbuilt; its first build attempt was killed before writing anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":928,"cache_read_input_tokens":135405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":928},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c90f1-c3ad-4e71-909e-30857e8a1663","uuid":"66de31b5-545f-4ea6-a12c-ffb87bdce406","timestamp":"2026-10-18T13:07:32.485Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9kgE5HBkFxo3pavt6oH"}
